    title: Deliver demand-gated accelerated-frame and elevator extension explorer
    outcome: Reconcile and deliver Issue 125 as a non-default, explicit-demand NLM
      extension with subject-owned elevator/pseudo-force/hanging-bob relations, one
      canonical accelerating-frame representation and learner explorer, without promoting
      R4 into ordinary Grade-9 completion scope.
    acceptance_statements:
    - R4 remains non-default and the accelerated-frame activity is explicitly demand-gated.
    - Elevator support, pseudo-force, and hanging-bob quantitative claims are gate-owned
      with explicit validity conditions.
    - The frame-choice microtopic binds one canonical representation and one authored
      activity using declared Physics representation kinds.
    - The explorer separates velocity from acceleration, preserves mg in free fall,
      applies pseudo-force only to accelerating-frame bookkeeping, and provides bounded
      hanging-bob transfer.
    - No circular-motion scope leak or default-route expansion is introduced.
    - Repository-wide guardrails pass and v31-relay validates against exact Common@1c168695f237a8bef184a9e189be80fab87d1e78.
